{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And this is the law of the sacrifice of the shelamim.</b> He informs us that even though all shelamim are offerings of lesser sanctity, there is nevertheless a distinction among them: if they are brought on account of thanksgiving, they must include a leavened offering placed within it. For although the cause of the danger on account of which the thanksgiving is offered is the leaven in the dough, nevertheless the varieties of unleavened bread outweigh it, and through the abundance of bread the miracle will be made known to many eaters — and all of them are eaten within the timeframe of most holy offerings, namely one day and a night."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:36.102133345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}